    <item>
      <title>2.11.0</title>
      <description>
        <![CDATA[
          <ul>
            <li>Ko-fi support card: about 20 seconds after you pick an item from the history (copy or paste), or a rule action finishes, a small receipt card may ask for a tip. It waits until 7 days after you install or update to this version, and until more than 60 picks from the history. It asks at most 3 times a year, only when you used the Mac in the last 10 seconds and are not typing, and never while the history popup, a MaccyPlus window, an update prompt or a menu is open, the screen is locked or the microphone is in use. "Ask me in 2 weeks" snoozes it. "Nope, don't ask again" keeps it quiet until the next major version, and for at least 90 days. A card still open when you open the history popup, a MaccyPlus window or an update prompt, or when the Mac sleeps or locks, closes and counts as a snooze; one left unanswered for 5 minutes, or 2 minutes without input, fades and counts as a snooze too. The card never takes keyboard focus, and the same three choices head the right-click menu while it shows, for keyboard and VoiceOver users. Hold ⌥ in the right-click menu for "Show Support Prompt Now" to preview it. The pick and rule-action counts (since this version) stay on your Mac, in the app's preferences; nothing is sent.</li>
          </ul>
        ]]>
      </description>
      <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:23:23 +0200</pubDate>
      <releaseNotesLink>https://github.com/roypadina/maccyplus/releases/tag/v2.11.0</releaseNotesLink>
